# Skilleraa — Project

## Overview
Student freelancing marketplace for beginners. Roles: **student**, **client**, **admin**.

## Vision
Help students get first paid work; help clients hire affordable early-career talent. Ship stable, secure SaaS — quality over speed.

## Tech stack (production truth)
| Layer | Tech |
|-------|------|
| Frontend | React 19, CRA+CRACO, Tailwind, React Router 7, TanStack Query, Supabase JS, Sonner, Framer Motion, Recharts (admin) |
| Backend | FastAPI, PyJWT, Supabase PostgREST (service role) |
| Data / Authz | Supabase Postgres + **RLS** (source of truth; no MongoDB) |
| Storage | Supabase Storage (`resumes`, `portfolios`) |
| Realtime | Supabase Realtime (messages) |
| Payments | Razorpay (INR) |
| Deploy | Vercel (frontend); API hosted separately |

Forms today: controlled inputs. Prefer `react-hook-form` + `zod` only when adding complex multi-step forms.

## Folder structure
```
frontend/src/{pages,components,context,lib}
backend/{server.py,payments_razorpay.py,storage_uploads.py}
api/index.py                 # Vercel Python entry
supabase/migrations/         # ordered SQL + RLS
.env.example                 # full template
```

## Environment variables
**Frontend only:** `REACT_APP_SUPABASE_URL`, `REACT_APP_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `REACT_APP_BACKEND_URL`  
**Backend secrets:** `SUPABASE_*` (incl. service role + JWT secret), `CORS_ORIGINS`, `RAZORPAY_*`, `LOG_LEVEL`  
Never put service role / JWT / Razorpay secret in the frontend. Do not set `MONGO_URL` (unused).

## Coding philosophy
- Extend existing modules; no drive-by rewrites or UI redesigns
- Supabase + RLS for product authz; FastAPI for payments, uploads, sync
- Production-ready: loading / empty / error states, a11y, mobile
- No secrets, no TODOs, no placeholders, no duplicate components/APIs

## CTO mandate
Operate as permanent CTO: protect production stability and long-term maintainability.

- Prefer clean architecture and low debt over shipping speed
- Optimize / reuse before adding complexity or new layers
- Reject bad implementations; never sacrifice quality for convenience
- When a request conflicts with architecture: **explain why**, then **propose a better path** — do not silently implement the worse option
- Think in years: authz, migrations, and APIs must stay safe to evolve
